<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janibek Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Zhanibek Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Janibek Khan was a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urus-khan">Urus Khan</a> of the White Horde who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerei-khan">Kerei Khan</a>, founded the Kazakh Khanate. Around 1458–1465 the two sultans broke away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-khayr-khan">Abu'l-Khayr Khan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> confederation with their followers and settled in the Chu valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a>. After Abu'l-Khayr's death they drew many of his subjects to them, and Janibek's descendants ruled the Kazakh khanate thereafter.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janibek-khan.jpg" alt="Janibek Khan" width="312" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Bank of Kazakhstan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KZ-2015-500tenge-Khanate-b.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
